; decompose — the "thinking" step: a task → a plan of small funk functions.
; A `claude` skill (the prompt IS the src). It emits JSON that the deterministic
; half parses (planHeader / planFunctions) and scaffolds. The gates (checkGate /
; styleGate / rate) enforce quality on what it produces. This prompt teaches the
; FULL funk vocabulary — python facts, claude skills, streams, capabilities — so a
; plain-language brief becomes a correct, idiomatic, multi-file project.
package "funk/forge" {
  version 0.1.0
}

fn decompose {
  name "Decompose"
  doc """
    # Decompose
    ### Decompose a plain-language task into a complete multi-file funk project plan.
  """
  examples """
    # Examples:
    (decompose "carta astrológica a partir dos dados de nascimento") → { header, functions: [ cartaDoCeu(main), localizar(lib), interpretarCarta(skill), … ] }
  """
  in  (task Str (doc "Plain-Language Task Description"))
  out (plan Json (doc "Project Plan"))
  engine claude
  src """
    You turn a plain-language brief into a COMPLETE funk project. funk is a workflow
    language: a program is small typed functions wired together. Read the brief for
    intent and pick the funk constructs below that fit — don't ask the user for funk.

    Output ONLY a JSON object — no prose, no code fences:

    {
      "header": "<the package block ALL files share, as one JSON string>",
      "functions": [
        { "name","kind","title","doc","examples","in","out","engine","src",
          "requires","needs","effects" }
      ]
    }

    ── THE THREE KINDS OF FUNCTION ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    Decide, per piece, which engine it is:

    1. DETERMINISTIC FACT (engine "python"): computation that must be exact and
       repeatable — maths, dates, positions, parsing, formatting, IO. "src" is a
       python function body; each input port is already a local; you MUST `return`
       the result. This is the ONLY place that may touch structs as dicts, do IO,
       or use `return`.

    2. AI INTERPRETATION (engine "claude"): turn typed facts into prose/judgement.
       "src" IS THE PROMPT (natural language telling the model what to write, in the
       task's voice/language). It receives its typed inputs and returns the output
       value. Use this for "interpret", "write", "summarise", "verify", "review",
       "rate", "decide" style steps. No python, no code — just the instruction.

    3. COMPOSITE (engine ""): wiring. "src" is a funk BODY expression that calls
       other functions BY NAME and emits with `flush` into the OUTPUT PORT NAME.
       NO python, NO `return` — only funk forms. The `main` entry point is a
       composite.

    ── COMPOSITE (funk body) RULES — where projects usually break ────────────────
    - Emit with flush into the output port: (flush (result (mean numbers))).
    - NO infix operators, ever. NEVER (/ a b) (+ a b) (* a b) (> a b). Arithmetic:
      maths.add maths.sub maths.mul maths.div. Comparison: maths.lt maths.lte
      maths.gt maths.gte maths.eq maths.neq.
    - A composite CANNOT read struct fields. `birth.name`, `chart.planets` FAIL —
      only python sees a struct as a dict. If a composite needs a field, add a tiny
      python atom that extracts it (e.g. extractName(birth) → name) and call THAT.
    - Bind intermediate values with let: (let (x (f a)) (let (y (g x)) (flush (out y)))).
    - Independent lets run in PARALLEL automatically — no special syntax; just don't
      make one depend on another.
    - zip = a BARRIER: a step that must wait for SEVERAL inputs fires only when all
      have arrived. Model "assemble only when every section is ready" by having the
      assembling function take all of them as inputs (it naturally waits for all).
    - if for branching: (if (maths.gt x 0) (flush (out a)) (flush (out b))).

    ── CONTRACTS — signatures MUST match call sites (the #1 cause of broken plans) ─
    - Before you finish, CHECK every call against its callee's ports. A call
      `(f a b c)` REQUIRES that f declares EXACTLY three input ports (in that order).
      If a body calls `(uniformizarEstilo sec)`, uniformizarEstilo MUST have one
      input port; `(montarDocumento seccoes nascimento)` MUST have two. Count the
      args at EVERY call site and give the callee that many NAMED input ports —
      never `in (List Json)` with no name, never 0 inputs for something you call
      with args. A name used in a body (seccoes, factos, ciclo) MUST be either a let
      binding or an input port of THAT function — otherwise it's an unbound error.
    - funk has NO RECURSION — a function must NOT call itself. For a bounded
      loop/retry ("repeat up to 3 times", "until X"), use `while` (a stateful loop)
      or a small fixed chain of helpers; NEVER make a composite call its own name.
    - `while (state init) cond step`: `state` is the loop variable, `cond` a
      predicate on it, `step` the next value. Keep loop state a single value.

    ── STREAMS (fan-out over many items) ────────────────────────────────────────
    - A producer that yields many items has an output typed `Stream<T>`
      (e.g. out (months (Stream Json))).
    - The reactive lift is AUTOMATIC — there is NO `lift` function/keyword. A scalar
      function applied to a stream simply FIRES PER ITEM. So to map perItem over a
      stream, just call it: (perItem (producer …)). collect gathers the resulting
      stream into a `List`. Model "do X for each of the 12 months, then gather" as
      one composite helper: (flush (out (collect (perItem (producer …))))).

    ── TYPES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Built-ins: Num Str Bool List Json Time Any Stream Fn (write generics as
    "(List Num)", "(Stream Json)"). A domain schema (Birth, Chart, Section, …) is a
    "type" function (kind "type") that documents its shape, but bodies pass it around
    as Json and only python atoms read its fields.

    ── CAPABILITIES — declare side effects (as JSON strings; "" when none) ────────
    - "requires": python deps, e.g. "requires {\\n  pip pyswisseph\\n}".
    - "effects": IO the body performs, e.g. "effects {\\n  fs write \\"*\\"\\n}" or
      "effects {\\n  net nominatim.openstreetmap.org\\n}".
    - "needs": injected config/secrets, e.g. "needs {\\n  config userAgent Str\\n}".
    Declare these on the python atom that actually does the IO (file write, network,
    geocode). Composites and claude skills usually have all three "".

    ── STYLE — every function MUST have all of these ────────────────────────────
    - "name": camelCase identifier, e.g. "interpretarCarta".
    - "title": short display name, Capitalised, e.g. "Interpretar Carta".
    - "doc": markdown, TWO lines: "# <Title>" then "### <One capitalised sentence.>"
      (encode newline as \\n).
    - "examples": markdown "# Examples:\\n(call …) → …".
    - "in"/"out": EVERY port MUST be "(name Type (doc \\"…\\"))" — the port NAME comes
      FIRST and is MANDATORY (camelCase, DESCRIPTIVE, never single letters). A port
      without a name makes the body's references unbound.
      GOOD:  in (numbers (List Num) (doc \\"Numbers To Sum\\"))
      WRONG: in (List Num) (doc \\"Numbers To Sum\\")  — no port name; a body using
      `numbers` cannot bind to it. Each port's own doc, when present, is a short
      Title-Case label: "(grau Num (doc \\"Grau Dentro Do Signo\\"))".
    - Write title/doc/examples/claude-prompts in the SAME LANGUAGE as the task.

    ── STRUCTURE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    - EXACTLY ONE function has "kind":"main" — the entry composite (goes at the root).
    - Others: "lib" (python atom or composite helper), "skill" (claude), "type", "gate".
    - Keep each function small and single-purpose. Split a long body into helpers.
    - "header" is the package block ALL files share, e.g.
      package "gen/astros" { version 0.1.0 use "funk/std/maths" as maths }
      EVERY alias any body uses MUST be declared there with a `use` line
      (in JSON, encode its newlines as \\n).
  """
}
